Requirement Analysis Phase
PocketSmart AI: Your Smart Budget & Recommendation Assistant

Requirement Analysis Phase

1. Introduction

The Requirement Analysis Phase is an important stage in the development of PocketSmart AI, a smart budgeting and recommendation assistant. In this phase, the requirements of users are identified, analyzed, documented, and organized.

PocketSmart AI is designed to help users manage their money, track expenses, create budgets, analyze spending habits, and receive personalized recommendations. The system uses AI-based analysis to provide useful suggestions based on the user's financial information.


---

2. Problem Statement

Many people find it difficult to manage their monthly income and expenses. Common problems include:

Lack of proper expense tracking.

Overspending on unnecessary items.

Difficulty creating a realistic budget.

Not knowing where most of their money is spent.

Difficulty identifying spending patterns.

Lack of personalized financial suggestions.

Managing expenses manually can be time-consuming.


Therefore, there is a need for a simple and intelligent application that can help users understand and manage their personal budgets.


---

3. Proposed Solution

PocketSmart AI provides a digital platform where users can enter their income and expenses. The system analyzes the information and presents useful financial insights.

The application can provide:

Income and expense tracking.

Monthly budget creation.

Expense categorization.

Spending analysis.

Budget alerts.

Savings suggestions.

AI-powered recommendations.

Dashboard with financial summaries.



---

4. Objectives

The main objectives of PocketSmart AI are:

1. To help users track their daily expenses.


2. To provide an easy way to create monthly budgets.


3. To categorize expenses automatically or manually.


4. To analyze users' spending patterns.


5. To identify unnecessary or excessive spending.


6. To provide personalized recommendations.


7. To encourage better saving habits.


8. To display financial information through a simple dashboard.




---

5. Functional Requirements

Functional requirements describe what the system should do.

5.1 User Management

User should be able to create an account.

User should be able to log in securely.

User should be able to manage their profile.


5.2 Income Management

Add income details.

Record different sources of income.

View total income for a selected period.


5.3 Expense Management

Add daily expenses.

Edit or delete expenses.

Enter expense amount, date, and category.

View previous transactions.


5.4 Expense Categorization

Expenses can be divided into categories such as:

Food

Transportation

Education

Shopping

Entertainment

Bills

Healthcare

Other


5.5 Budget Management

Set a monthly budget.

Set category-wise spending limits.

Display remaining budget.

Compare actual spending with planned spending.


5.6 AI Recommendation System

The AI component analyzes the user's financial data and provides suggestions such as:

Areas where the user spends more.

Possible ways to reduce unnecessary expenses.

Suggested spending limits.

Savings suggestions.

Personalized budget recommendations.


5.7 Dashboard

The dashboard should display:

Total income.

Total expenses.

Remaining balance.

Budget usage.

Major expense categories.

Savings information.

AI recommendations.


5.8 Notifications and Alerts

The system can notify users when:

Spending approaches a budget limit.

A category exceeds its planned budget.

Unusual spending is detected.

A monthly budget needs attention.



---

6. Non-Functional Requirements

Non-functional requirements describe how the system should perform.

Performance

The application should respond quickly when users add or view financial information.

Security

User financial information should be protected from unauthorized access.

Usability

The interface should be simple and easy for beginners to understand.

Reliability

The system should store and retrieve transaction information accurately.

Scalability

The application should be capable of supporting more users and transactions in the future.

Maintainability

The source code should be organized so that new features can easily be added.

Compatibility

The application should work properly on commonly used browsers and devices.


---

7. Hardware Requirements

Minimum hardware requirements may include:

Processor: Intel Core i3 or equivalent

RAM: 4 GB or above

Storage: 10 GB free space

Internet connection

Smartphone or computer for accessing the application



---

8. Software Requirements

Possible software requirements include:

Frontend: HTML, CSS, JavaScript

Backend: Python / Flask

Database: SQLite or MySQL

AI: Google Gemini API

Development Environment: Visual Studio Code

Browser: Google Chrome / Microsoft Edge

Version Control: Git and GitHub



---

9. User Requirements

The user should be able to:

1. Register and log in.


2. Enter income details.


3. Add and manage expenses.


4. Select expense categories.


5. Set monthly budgets.


6. View financial summaries.


7. Analyze spending habits.


8. Receive AI-based recommendations.


9. Monitor budget limits.


10. View previous transactions.




---

10. AI Requirements

The AI module should analyze available financial information and generate understandable recommendations.

For example:

Input:
Monthly income = ₹25,000
Food expenses = ₹8,000
Transportation = ₹3,000
Shopping = ₹6,000

AI Output:
“Your food and shopping expenses form a significant portion of your recorded spending. Consider setting category-wise limits and reviewing non-essential purchases.”

The recommendations should be presented as general budgeting guidance, not as professional financial advice.


---

11. Data Requirements

The system may store:

Data	Description

User ID	Unique user identification
Name	User name
Email	User email
Income	Income amount
Expense	Expense amount
Category	Expense category
Date	Transaction date
Budget	Planned spending amount
Balance	Remaining amount
Recommendation	AI-generated suggestion



---

12. System Constraints

Internet may be required for AI-based features.

AI recommendations depend on the quality of user-provided data.

The application should protect sensitive financial information.

AI-generated recommendations may not always be perfectly accurate.

The system should not claim to provide professional investment or financial advice.



---

13. Expected Outcome

After completing the Requirement Analysis Phase, the project team will have a clear understanding of:

What PocketSmart AI should do.

Who will use the system.

What data is required.

What technologies can be used.

What functional features need to be developed.

What security and performance requirements must be considered.


Conclusion

The Requirement Analysis Phase establishes the foundation for PocketSmart AI. By clearly identifying user needs, functional requirements, technical requirements, and system constraints, the development team can proceed to the Design Phase with a well-defined understanding of the proposed application.
